    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math education—adapting explanations to a student’s level, pace, and interests. They can turn abstract concepts into stories or visual metaphors, like linking derivatives to slopes in a narrative. For teachers, they save time on repetitive tasks, letting them focus on deeper understanding and creativity."
